{
    "background_story": "Henrik was a wealthy entrepreneur who made his fortune in the tech industry. However, his true passion lay in horse racing. Every summer, he would escape to Saratoga Springs, New York, to indulge in the thrill of the track. Henrik owned a few prized thoroughbreds, which he would enter into the prestigious Saratoga Cup. His love for the sport was matched only by his love for the charming town, with its rich history and picturesque scenery. As a prominent figure in the Saratoga racing community, Henrik was known for his generosity and sportsmanship. He would often host lavish parties at his estate, where he would regale guests with tales of his racing triumphs and the beauty of Saratoga. For Henrik, Saratoga was more than just a place \u2013 it was a state of mind, a symbol of elegance and excitement.",
